SCOPE: RF1 attempt 2 (worktree /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/.claude/worktrees/retiree-refresh,
branch feat/retiree-refresh off master 344cb30). Manifest files: tailwind.config.js,
web/static/css/styles.css, web/static/js/charts.js, web/static/css/tailwind.css,
web/templates/layouts/base.html, web/templates/components/shared/range-picker.html.
No RF1.1.checker-a11y.verdict existed to reuse (only RF1.1.checker-second.verdict did);
this is a from-scratch render-based audit of attempt 2. Diff vs master confirmed with
`/usr/bin/git diff master -- <path>` for every manifest file before testing (all match
RF-RUN-SPEC item 1-6 exactly, including the attempt-2-only change: the three desktop
group-label spans get `hidden 2xl:inline` with ids kept).

METHOD: Built branch server (isolated data copy) via `scripts/whatif-verify.sh start 8142`
(never :8080/:8081). Master baseline: `cp -a` to scratch
/tmp/claude-1000/.../scratchpad/rf1-a11y2, `git checkout master -- web tailwind.config.js`
in that COPY ONLY, `make css`, built + started on 8152 via the same script (REPO derived
from the copy's own path). Both `curl /api/health` OK throughout. Playwright per given
paths/args; dark mode tested both ways: (a) cold-load via `page.addInitScript` setting
`localStorage.theme='dark'` before navigation (matches base.html's inline
head script, the realistic persisted-preference path) and (b) a real click on
`#theme-toggle` (dispatches the `themechange` event charts.js/insights.js listen for).
NOTE: a raw `documentElement.classList.toggle('dark')` post-load WITHOUT re-navigation
or the themechange event (the literal wording in my own dispatch brief) does NOT
re-render already-drawn Plotly charts, because charts.js/insights.js key their redraw
on the `themechange` CustomEvent, not a class-attribute MutationObserver — using it
produced spurious "black chart text on dark card" hits I discarded after confirming
(check-real-toggle.js, check-coldload-dark.js) that both real user paths (persisted
dark cold-load, and clicking the toggle) redraw with the correct RF1 colors. Recording
this so the method is auditable, per instructions to attribute methodology explicitly.

1. AXE (wcag2a/2aa/21aa/22aa), all 9 pages x 1440/390 x light/dark, every <details> opened:
   `node audit2.js` (page.goto waitUntil:'load' + 600ms settle; networkidle hung
   indefinitely on /whatif's polling and was abandoned after it took down the 8142
   server under the first attempt — confirmed not reproducible with plain curl calls
   afterward, i.e. a Playwright/networkidle artifact, not a server crash under normal
   load).
   RESULT — branch violations found: /transfers 390 (`scrollable-region-focusable`,
   1 node, both themes) and /major-expenses 390 (`target-size`, 6 nodes, both themes).
   Master has the IDENTICAL two (same rule ids, same node counts). ACCESSIBILITY.md's
   own RF.0 "Deferred" list names both as pre-existing/out-of-territory. Not a RF1 FAIL.
   /dashboard 390: master has `scrollable-region-focusable` (2 nodes, both themes);
   BRANCH HAS ZERO — RF4 (accepted, dashboard.js chart-table wrapper a11y attrs) already
   cured this on the branch; OBSERVATION, not attributable to RF1 (different manifest).
   Every other page (dashboard@1440, insights, whatif, explorer, accounts, filemanager,
   duplicates) is axe-clean on both branch and master, both sizes, both themes.
   Insights June-range + all 5 sub-tabs (trends/income/anomalies/pricecreep/pace) x
   1440/390 x light/dark: `node insights-june.js` — 0 violations everywhere, branch and
   master identical.
   => No violation introduced or replicated by RF1. PASS.

2. Manual contrast walk (point 7/12), /dashboard, /insights(June), /whatif, /explorer,
   /accounts, both themes, real dark-mode paths: `node contrast-walk3.js` (treewalker
   over every visible text node incl. SVG <text> via `fill` not `color`; background
   resolved incl. `background-image` gradients, composited through the ancestor chain;
   large-text threshold 3:1 else 4.5:1). Findings, each cross-checked branch vs master:
   - Active nav-tab white text vs the accent-strong pill overlay: 4.19:1 on BOTH branch
     and master (rgb(114,107,234) composited bg either way) — the active-tab background
     classes (`bg-white/20` over `bg-gradient-to-r from-accent-strong`) are untouched by
     RF1 (only `px-3`->`px-2` + `whitespace-nowrap` changed, no color class). PRE-EXISTING,
     unowned. OBSERVATION for backlog (borderline WCAG 1.4.3 miss, not new).
   - Dashboard "34.3%" annotation text, light mode: ratio 1.0 on both branch and master
     (same off-visual-layer text, identical in both). PRE-EXISTING/harness-neutral.
   - Dashboard "Target $11351" chart annotation, dark mode: 3.14:1 branch vs 3.04:1
     master (marginally IMPROVED by the stone remap, not worsened) — the annotation
     itself is rendered by dashboard.js/Plotly defaults, not an RF1-owned file.
     PRE-EXISTING, unowned, and not made worse.
   - Whatif "$" prefix span (`text-gray-600` with no `dark:` variant), dark mode: 1.99:1
     branch vs 1.94:1 master — same missing-dark-variant defect on both (whatif.html is
     not in RF1's manifest); warm-grey remap changes the number negligibly, doesn't
     newly break it (already broken). PRE-EXISTING, unowned.
   - Accounts sr-only captions/TH ("Balance anchors for...", "Actions"): visually
     clipped (sr-only), not rendered to sighted users — contrast is moot for hidden
     text (not a WCAG 1.4.3 subject); present identically on both. Non-issue.
   => No new contrast failure on any of the five pages in either theme. PASS.

3. Nav (points 1/3/9, WCAG 1.3.1/4.1.2), branch server: `node nav-check2.js`.
   - 1280px: `getComputedStyle(#nav-group-money/plan/setup).display` = `none` (labels
     hidden per the attempt-2 fix) but `page.getByRole('group', {name:'Money'/'Plan'/
     'Setup', exact:true})` each resolve to count=1 — Playwright's accessible-name
     computation (which follows the same algorithm a screen reader uses) confirms
     `aria-labelledby` pointing at a `display:none` element still resolves the name.
     Confirmed via the real accessibility-name API, not just DOM inspection.
   - 1280px, WITH the production Duplicates badge injected into the live DOM (`<a
     href="/duplicates">` + count badge, exact production markup, inserted after File
     Manager): `documentElement.scrollWidth == documentElement.clientWidth == 1280` —
     no overflow. All 9 desktop nav links (incl. "Duplicates3") share the same `top`
     (14.9px) and the same `height` (38.3px, one line — not 2x line-height). Header's
     own right edge == 1280 == window width.
   - 1536px: labels `display:block`, all three group names still resolve via
     `getByRole`, no overflow (`scrollWidth==clientWidth==1536`).
   - Mobile menu (390px) markup untouched (confirmed by the diff — RF1 edited only the
     `hidden xl:flex` desktop block).
   - Keyboard order unchanged (class-only edits, same anchor order/count as master).
   => PASS (this is the ruling RF-2026-09-07c fix under direct verification, not just
   accepted on the second checker's earlier evidence).

4. Focus rings (point 9): indigo-500 vs new dark card recomputed independently —
   `python3` sRGB relative-luminance calc: indigo-500 #6366f1 vs stone-900 #1c1917 =
   3.92:1, vs stone-800 #292524 = 3.40:1 — matches charts.js's own updated comment
