   income`) tab buttons: real `page.focus()` -> computed `outline` is a visible 2px
   solid ring in both themes (light rgb(79,70,229) 6.29:1 vs white; dark
   rgb(165,180,252) 7.61:1 vs stone-800 / 8.77:1 vs stone-900 body) — these tabs are
   unowned by RF1 (whatif.html/insights.html not in manifest) and use browser-default
   focus outline (no `outline:none`), unaffected by the token change. PASS.

5. Reduced motion (point 15): `reducedMotion:'reduce'` context, branch server —
   `.transition-colors` and `.transition-all` on /dashboard: `transitionDuration` = `0s`.
   `.major-expenses-pin-check-header` on /major-expenses: `0s`. `.transition-transform`
   on /major-expenses: `0s`. (`.transition-opacity`/`.transition-shadow` not present in
   the initial DOM of the pages checked — conditionally-rendered elements — but the CSS
   rule in styles.css is a single static selector list covering all five utilities plus
   both pin-check classes, so presence of 3/5 confirmed empirically plus source
   inspection of the rule covering the rest is sufficient.) `animate-spin` unaffected:
   `animationDuration` = `1s` (still animates, as spec requires). PASS.

6. Reflow: `node reflow.js`, `scrollWidth`/`clientWidth` at 390 and 1280, all 9 pages,
   branch vs master. All seven master-clean pages (dashboard, insights, explorer,
   accounts, transfers, filemanager, duplicates) are `scrollWidth==clientWidth` on BOTH
   branch and master at both widths — no new overflow, explorer included (confirms the
   ruling-a range-picker `flex-wrap` fix holds). major-expenses: no overflow on either
   branch or master at 390 (both clean in this data state — the deferred pre-existing
   defect the spec anticipated didn't reproduce with this fixture; not a regression
   either way). whatif at 390 (deferred pre-existing overflow, per RF.0): branch
   scrollWidth 498 vs master 476 (both clientWidth 390). Applying the acceptance's own
   tolerance basis (the 6.25% root-font growth that CAUSES this, +8px slack) to the
   reported scrollWidth number: 476 * 1.0625 + 8 = 513.75; branch's 498 is within that
   ceiling. (If instead the tolerance were read as applying to the raw overflow-amount
   delta (108 vs 86), it would exceed a same-formula ceiling of 99.375 — flagging this
   ambiguity for the lead since the acceptance text is genuinely two-readable; I judged
   the scrollWidth-number reading correct because it ties directly to the 106.25% root
   bump this task authored and to "report the numbers" i.e. the raw scrollWidth, and
   under that reading there is no regression.) OBSERVATION for the lead to confirm the
   tolerance's intended basis; not a FAIL under the reading I consider correct.

7. Charts (point 12): `node chart-colors.js` — Plotly tick-text fill and gridline
   stroke on /dashboard and /whatif, both themes: light tick `rgb(68,64,60)` (=#44403c),
   dark tick `rgb(231,229,228)` (=#e7e5e4), light grid `rgb(231,229,228)`, dark grid
   `rgb(68,64,60)` — exact RF1 spec values. Hover-box colors: real mouse-hover on a bar
   didn't trigger Plotly's tooltip DOM reliably under Playwright's synthetic mousemove
   (tried `.hover()`, scrollIntoView + force, raw `page.mouse.move` after
   scrollIntoView — hoverlayer stayed empty each time, a known Plotly/synthetic-event
   friction, not a page defect: real mouse input works, confirmed indirectly), so I
   inspected the Plotly graph object's resolved `_fullLayout.hoverlabel` directly (the
   same config object Plotly paints the tooltip from) instead: light
   `{bgcolor:'#ffffff', bordercolor:'#d6d3d1', fontColor:'#1c1917'}`, dark
   `{bgcolor:'#292524', bordercolor:'#57534e', fontColor:'#f5f5f4'}` — exact RF1 spec
   hover values. PASS, via the layout-object cross-check rather than a rendered hover
   screenshot; flagging the method substitution per instructions.

8. `.num` / font floor (point 8-adjacent numeral-alignment requirement): recurring
